    <section class="page-hero section-soft">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h1>Verify. Fund. Deliver. Prove.</h1>
        <p class="lead-small">Everything RallyGood does is organised around one repeatable product: the Drop.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell">
        <h2 class="sr-only">The four steps of a Drop</h2>
        <div class="steps-grid four">
          <article class="step-card"><span>01</span><h3>Verify</h3><p>Before any Drop opens we confirm the need, the local partner, the costs, the delivery route, the risks and how evidence will be collected.</p></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span>02</span><h3>Fund</h3><p>A Drop is published with a target, a cost breakdown and a named partner. People give, share and fundraise in teams.</p></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span>03</span><h3>Deliver</h3><p>Funds are paid to the partner under agreed controls. The partner buys locally or regionally where possible and delivers the essentials.</p></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span>04</span><h3>Prove</h3><p>We publish a close-out report: what was raised, what was spent, what was delivered, what went wrong and what we learned. See <a class="text-link" href="transparency.html">what we will publish</a>.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

