        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">If a target is missed or exceeded</p>
          <h2>Clear rules, before you give.</h2>
          <p class="lead-small">Money given to a Drop is for that Drop. We will tell donors in advance what happens if things change:</p>
          <ul class="plain-list">
            <li><strong>If we raise more than needed:</strong> surplus is used for the next similar appeal.</li>
            <li><strong>If we raise less:</strong> the Drop may be partially funded, extended, or funds offered back.</li>
            <li><strong>If a Drop is cancelled:</strong> donors are told straight away and offered a refund or a choice of another Drop.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-dark">
      <div class="shell split-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow light">Dignity-first promise</p>
          <h2>No pity marketing. Just practical help with proof.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="lead-small">We tell the truth about need without exploiting suffering. We will not publish photos or exact locations that could put people at risk, and we ask for consent before sharing images. Read our <a class="text-link light" href="safeguarding.html">safeguarding approach</a>.</p>
          <p class="lead-small"><strong>What we will not do:</strong> claim to be first responders, ship random goods from the UK, or launch a Drop that cannot be verified, costed and reported.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
